          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: आलुकम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आलुकम् — ālukam — \"a potato\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "āluka is ālu with the suffix -ka, an old word-list name for an edible root, the elephant-foot yam (CDIAL 1388). The potato reached India from the Americas only in modern times, and the languages moved the old name onto it: Hindi ālū \"potato\" (CDIAL 1388). MW gives no source for ālu, so its origin is uncertain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
