        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vṛntāka \"the aubergine\" is one of several Sanskrit names for the plant gathered in CDIAL 9369. CDIAL 11503 thinks the names probably share one origin and, after LM, gives it as Dravidian, while DEDR 5301 lists vṛntāka beside Dravidian words for the brinjal. Its sister form vātiṅgaṇa travelled west as Persian bādingān and lives on as Hindi baigan (CDIAL 11503)."
            }
          ]
        },
